		<title>By: Shivadam</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=955&#038;cpage=1#comment-24153</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Shivadam]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 05 Jun 2014 07:55:14 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=955#comment-24153</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Wow. I actually met &quot;ManWoman&quot; (the only of his names I heard that night) once - at an art gallery show in Phoenix - LONG before I had heard anything about the Dances of Universal Peace. I will never forget, and have sometimes shared, the one thing I remember him explaining in the brief moment I stood before him: about the tattoo on his forehead, he said: &quot;It weeds out the people I don&#039;t want to talk to anyway.&quot; Live on, ManWoman! And thank you. May the swastika be known only for the auspicious symbol it continues to be.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Wow. I actually met &#8220;ManWoman&#8221; (the only of his names I heard that night) once &#8211; at an art gallery show in Phoenix &#8211; LONG before I had heard anything about the Dances of Universal Peace. I will never forget, and have sometimes shared, the one thing I remember him explaining in the brief moment I stood before him: about the tattoo on his forehead, he said: &#8220;It weeds out the people I don&#8217;t want to talk to anyway.&#8221; Live on, ManWoman! And thank you. May the swastika be known only for the auspicious symbol it continues to be.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
