		<pubDate>Wed, 14 Nov 2012 21:29:44 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=955#comment-13486</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[In the last weeks my heart has been so much with Astarte and Manny, and Manny&#039;s cousin Patsy Wahita. Many visions of Manny were coming to me...him in his yellow, in the dance circle, with little murmurs of comments on this or that. His poetry readings at Koolaree, with his yellow cap and flowing gold-tinged hair in the dim light. I can hear his voice, his laughter, and see those yellow crocs and imagine his grace in passing beyond. He leaves a strong imprint on my heart and my love goes out to all who have been close to him. Alhamdulillah!]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>In the last weeks my heart has been so much with Astarte and Manny, and Manny&#8217;s cousin Patsy Wahita. Many visions of Manny were coming to me&#8230;him in his yellow, in the dance circle, with little murmurs of comments on this or that. His poetry readings at Koolaree, with his yellow cap and flowing gold-tinged hair in the dim light. I can hear his voice, his laughter, and see those yellow crocs and imagine his grace in passing beyond. He leaves a strong imprint on my heart and my love goes out to all who have been close to him. Alhamdulillah!</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: Khadija Goforth</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=955&#038;cpage=1#comment-13483</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Khadija Goforth]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 14 Nov 2012 16:07:52 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=955#comment-13483</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Well, our blessed brother has leapt back into the mystery from whence he came. Again and again, with words, images and silence Manny extended a &quot;ticket to be outrageous,&quot; often freeing those encountering him in ways unknown to them, or even to him.
I often revisit the story of his &quot;spiritual awakening,&quot; finding courage in his facing the crumbling of his false self in response to the compelling sacred light calling forth his deepest self. A natural dervish doorway to &quot;the real,&quot; Manny&#039;s life demonstrated a sincere response to God&#039;s call.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Well, our blessed brother has leapt back into the mystery from whence he came. Again and again, with words, images and silence Manny extended a &#8220;ticket to be outrageous,&#8221; often freeing those encountering him in ways unknown to them, or even to him.<br />
I often revisit the story of his &#8220;spiritual awakening,&#8221; finding courage in his facing the crumbling of his false self in response to the compelling sacred light calling forth his deepest self. A natural dervish doorway to &#8220;the real,&#8221; Manny&#8217;s life demonstrated a sincere response to God&#8217;s call.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
